message: "If you use this dataset, please cite it as below."
title: "PnPCorrespondences: Synthetic 2D-3D Point Correspondences for Camera Calibration and PnP Benchmarking"
abstract: >-
  A large, systematic, image-free dataset of 2D-3D point correspondences with
  exact ground truth, for benchmarking camera calibration, Perspective-n-Point
  solvers, robust estimators and bundle adjustment. Structured 3D scenes are
  projected through pinhole, Brown-Conrady and Kannala-Brandt camera models over
  a wide range of fields of view and sensor resolutions, then perturbed by
  controlled Gaussian pixel noise, pixel quantization and outlier contamination
  from 0 to 95 per cent in three modes. Every sample stores the 3D points, the
  noisy 2D observations, the exact intrinsics, lens distortion and extrinsics
  that produced them, and a ground-truth outlier mask, serialised to HDF5 with a
  Parquet manifest. Every array is a deterministic function of a master seed, so
  the dataset can be regenerated bit-for-bit. The accompanying generator, which
  is released under the MIT licence, also provides fifteen classical and modern
  PnP solvers, single-view and multi-view calibration baselines, evaluation
  metrics and reproducible benchmark tables.
